# InputSwitcher Support

InputSwitcher automatically switches to the input method assigned to the active Mac app.

## Getting started

1. Click the InputSwitcher keyboard icon in the macOS menu bar.
2. Open Settings and select Rules.
3. Add an application and choose its input method.
4. Enable Auto-Switch.

The rule is applied whenever you switch to that application.

## Common questions

### The input method did not change

Make sure Auto-Switch is enabled, the application has a rule, and the selected input source is installed and available in macOS. You can also use the menu bar shortcut to test the rule manually.

### How do I move my rules?

Use Rule Export and Rule Import from Settings. Professional users can also enable iCloud Sync to keep rules available on Macs signed in to the same Apple ID.

### How do I restore my Pro purchase?

Open the Pro settings page and choose Restore Purchases. Make sure you are signed in to the Apple ID used for the purchase.

## Contact and bug reports

Please [open an issue on GitHub](https://github.com/wxuesong/InputSwitcher/issues) with your macOS version, InputSwitcher version, and a description of the problem. Do not include passwords, typed text, or other private information.

